# Ward Flow preservation copies are byte-for-byte evidence of another checkout's
# uncommitted work, and `durableDirtyArtifactManifest` re-verifies each committed
# blob against the live original with `originalBytes.equals(preserved.bytes)`.
# The `* text=auto eol=lf` rule above would silently rewrite CRLF sources on the
# way in — measured 2026-08-31: 2 of Ward Board's 139 temporary files were CRLF
# and staged with different hashes than the files they were copied from. Store
# this tree verbatim so a preservation copy cannot be normalised into a lie.
docs/ward-flow/control/evidence/artifacts/** -text

# Recovery bundles are hash-critical evidence and must never be filtered on the way in or out.
docs/ward-flow/control/evidence/bundles/** -text

# The versioned lesson copy is compared BYTE-FOR-BYTE against a machine-local store.
# Line-ending normalisation would make every CRLF lesson differ on a fresh checkout and
# leave `sync-lessons.mjs --check` permanently red — and a check that can never pass gets
# switched off, which is one of the lessons in these very files.
docs/ward-flow/lessons/** -text
